ffmpeg-dmo (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase the edition's series onto deb-multimedia's 10:9.1-dmo1
    (FFmpeg 9.1, the release tarball checked against FFmpeg's release
    key), whose packaging is taken whole: libcurl, the obsolete opengl
    option dropped, the install globs.
  * Keep the side data values the edition published in +15:
    AV_FRAME_DATA_DOWNMIX_MATRIX, AV_FRAME_DATA_GAIN_MAP_PARAMS and
    AV_PKT_DATA_GAIN_MAP_PARAMS, new in FFmpeg 9.1, follow the edition's
    entries, so programs built against +15 to +17 read the same values.
  * Keep xfade easing: deb-multimedia's 02_vf_xfade-3.6.6.patch, which
    its 9.1 build drops because it no longer applies, refreshed without
    its slide wrap-around hunks (FFmpeg 9.1 has 16a4ce48c for them), and
    the header copied again by debian/rules.
  * Drop 03_fix-padding-in-mp3.patch, as deb-multimedia does: FFmpeg 9.1
    holds it (23fccd657c, Romain Beauxis).
  * Port 0031, 0035 (one auxC reader: the edition's with FFmpeg 9.1's
    gain map and alpha flags), 0042, 0053 (now the edition's ca5dbc9 in
    its original form), 0075, hb-A05, hb-A15 (with FFmpeg 9.1's
    pgssubdec fixes e3d24a4a1 and bfba88103 by Michael Niedermayer) and
    hb-A24; raise libavutil's minor version for 0076 and 0089 from 9.1's
    61.19. Refresh the context of 20 more; 76 apply as they are.
  * Give the edition's ten packet side data types FFmpeg 9.1's handles,
    so the side_data bitstream filter can name them.
  * Bring nine FATE references of the edition's tests to what the
    programs print: two persistence tests and three MPEG-TS tests take
    FFmpeg 9.1's ffprobe output (42b8f75a6b, 88f7fd9ec5); the depth SEI
    references take the fields 0090 prints, the MP4 depth track
    reference the titl box hb-A02 writes (stale since +15 and +16; the
    three tests failed on +17 too), and 9.1's AVIF alpha grid test the
    AuxId 0035 exports on the alpha tiles.
  * Keep Fraunhofer's xHE-AAC library, new in deb-multimedia's 9.1 build,
    with libfdk-aac behind the pkg.ffmpeg-dmo.fdk profile: both are
    non-free and stay out of the packages that are shipped.
  * HandBrake's FFmpeg fixes are part of the recipe's series.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
